preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"the migration notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade"},"233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"The complete values reference is maintained in `charts/lamassu/VALUES.md` in the Helm repository."},"234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"page","content":"Expose the Gateway","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking"},"235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","content":"Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways."},"236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"Expose the Lamassu Gateway"},"237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"What if you need three Gateways?"},"243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Verify the traffic path"},"245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."},"246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"External reachability is the result of the whole path. A `Gateway` resource alone does not configure your router, firewall, DNS, cloud load balancer or upstream NAT."},"247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Usually, no. If you omit it, the Gateway controller and the cluster load-balancer implementation can assign an address and report it in `Gateway.status.addresses` and the generated Service status."},"248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Set it only when:"},"249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"your cloud or bare-metal load balancer supports requesting a specific address"},"250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"that address is allocated to this Gateway"},"251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"the surrounding network already routes traffic for it to the cluster"},"252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."},"253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Keep these two settings separate:"},"254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`gateway.addresses` requests an address for the Gateway."},"255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."},"256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"If users connect by DNS name, put that name in `tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.hostnames`. Do not copy an upstream proxy's public IP into `gateway.addresses`."},"257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"For a small VM running K3s or MicroK8s, use one external Lamassu Gateway and route every Lamassu endpoint through it:"},"258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"This design uses one IP, one TLS entry point and one pair of ports. The chart already creates the required routes."},"259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."},"260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"For the recommended design:"},"261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Use only one externally exposed Lamassu Gateway."},"262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Ensure ports 80 and 443 are free. Disable or reconfigure Traefik if it is not part of your traffic path."},"263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Allow those ports through the VM firewall and any upstream security group."},"264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Point DNS at the VM's reachable address."},"265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"See the K3s ServiceLB documentation for its host-port behavior and how to replace it with another load-balancer implementation."},"266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."},"267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"An external public address can forward TCP 80 and 443 to the VM or to a Kubernetes-side VIP:"},"268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"The public IP belongs to the external device. Leave `gateway.addresses` unset or set it to the actual Kubernetes-side address, never to an address that the cluster cannot bind."},"269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"First decide whether you need three independent data planes or only three hostnames."},"270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Requirement"},"271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Recommended design"},"272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Consequence"},"273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Several Lamassu URLs or services"},"274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One Gateway with multiple routes"},"275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One IP and one proxy fleet; this is the chart default"},"276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways and separate external IPs"},"277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One VIP per Gateway"},"278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"},"279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways on one node and one IP"},"280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."},"289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway normally provisions a proxy fleet per `Gateway`. Its merged-Gateway mode can share one fleet and address, but it is not a drop-in switch for multiple Lamassu releases: the generated Lamassu listeners use the same ports and protocols without distinct hostnames, so they conflict unless you deliberately customize the listener design."},"290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"},"291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."},"292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If one Gateway can own TLS and routing, use the chart default."},"293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If Gateways need independent policy and you can allocate IPs, use one VIP per Gateway."},"294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If only the Kubernetes resources need separation, evaluate merged-Gateway mode and make every listener tuple unique."},"295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If data planes and TLS termination must stay independent behind one IP, add a front-door SNI passthrough layer."},"296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If none of those are possible, use different external ports or change the external network design."},"297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Check, in order:"},"298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"`Gateway` has `Accepted=True` and `Programmed=True`."},"299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Its status contains the expected address."},"300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The generated `LoadBalancer` Service has a usable external address."},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Port 443 reaches that address from the client network."},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"DNS resolves to the externally reachable endpoint."},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The certificate contains the DNS name or IP used by the client."},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The Gateway API treats addresses as desired state that a controller may assign or reject; see the Gateway API overview for the resource model."},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"page","content":"Kubernetes self-managed","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview"},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","content":"Choose an installation workflow and network architecture for Lamassu on your Kubernetes cluster."},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#self-managed-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Self-managed Kubernetes deployment"},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-an-installation-workflow","content":"Choose an installation workflow"},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-chart-provides","content":"What the Lamassu chart provides"},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#how-the-deployment-fits-together","content":"How the deployment fits together"},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#platform-requirements","content":"Platform requirements"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-the-next-page","content":"Choose the next page"},"313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#self-managed-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Run Lamassu in a Kubernetes cluster operated by your team. The Helm chart deploys the Lamassu services and their routing resources; you provide the cluster, persistent storage, identity provider, PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and the network path used by clients."},"314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-an-installation-workflow","content":"Workflow"},"315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-an-installation-workflow","content":"Use it for"},"316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self-hosted/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/deployment/self