and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Cascading revocation"},"618":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Checks after the change"},"619":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"The hierarchy determines the blast radius of any error or compromise. A root signs intermediate CAs; intermediates issue the identities used by devices and services. This separation lets you isolate environments and rotate a branch without replacing all trust."},"620":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"For a production installation, use a very restricted root and one or more operational intermediates. Separate intermediates when any of these boundaries change:"},"621":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"environment, such as production and preproduction;"},"622":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"owner or operating team;"},"623":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"device family or manufacturing process;"},"624":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"region or regulatory requirement;"},"625":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"cryptographic engine or key policy;"},"626":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"maintenance window and renewal cadence."},"627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"Avoid deep hierarchies without a concrete need. Each level adds chain distribution, validation and one more certificate you must renew."},"628":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"A child CA and its end-entity certificates must expire before their issuer. Reserve a margin that allows distributing another chain and renewing dependent certificates."},"629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Reissuing a CA** creates a new certificate over the existing key. Lamassu generates a CSR with that key, self-signs it if it is a root or asks the parent CA to sign it if it is subordinate. The new certificate becomes active and the CA points to its serial number; the old and new certificates are linked through metadata."},"630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Rotating a CA** creates a successor key and authority. It is the right choice in the face of compromise, a cryptographic change, an engine migration or non-exportable key policies."},"631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"Lamassu does not allow reissuing an already-revoked CA or a CA whose expiration date has passed. Plan ahead for both conditions."},"632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Reissue if the key is still trustworthy and you only need another validity period or an updated certificate."},"633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Rotate the key if compromise is suspected, the algorithm changes or you want to move custody to another engine."},"634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Create a parallel branch if you cannot update all consumers at the same time."},"635":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Revoke immediately only when the risk of keeping the CA outweighs the impact of interrupting the fleet."},"636":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#inventory-the-dependencies","content":"Locate child CAs, issued certificates, DMSs, connectors and external trust stores. Include devices that may stay offline for weeks or months."},"637":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#create-the-successor-ca","content":"Generate a new key in the planned engine, create the CA and assign it an explicit profile. Do not reuse the operational identifier to hide that it is a different generation."},"638":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#distribute-the-new-trust","content":"Add the new root or chain to consumers before issuing with it. In a DMS, use the managed CAs of `/cacerts` to temporarily keep both the old and new chains."},"639":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#switch-issuance","content":"Update the enrollment CA and profile of the DMSs. Keep the additional validation CAs if old certificates still need to be accepted during re-enrollment."},"640":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#renew-in-batches","content":"Migrate a small cohort, validate mTLS, OCSP and CRL from the consumer and expand progressively. Monitor which devices still present the old chain."},"641":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#close-the-overlap","content":"Once no legitimate consumer depends on the previous authority, remove it from issuance and from the distributed CAs. Revoke it if policy requires it."},"642":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"When you revoke a CA, Lamassu also updates its child CAs and issued certificates to `REVOKED` with the reason `CessationOfOperation`. The children's revocations propagate the effect to their own branches."},"643":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"This protects the coherence of the hierarchy, but it makes revocation a high-impact action. Do not use it as the ordinary mechanism to stop issuing: first complete the migration and remove the CA from operational flows."},"644":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The new chain ends in an anchor installed by the consumer."},"645":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"New certificates contain the expected AKI, SKI, KU, EKU and SAN."},"646":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The DMS delivers the correct chain through EST `/cacerts`."},"647":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Re-enrollment accepts the old identity during the planned period."},"648":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"OCSP and CRL respond for the authorities that remain active."},"649":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"No DMS is left accidentally issuing from the old CA."},"650":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"See the Trust model to understand the DMS's CA sets and Certificate lifecycle for states and revocation effects."},"651":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"page","content":"Certification authorities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities"},"652":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"Create, import and operate the authori