latform/pki/ocsp"},"2168":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Check in real time whether a certificate is still valid or has been revoked."},"2169":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP service"},"2170":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"2171":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"2172":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"2173":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"2174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"2175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP (Online Certificate Status Protocol) is the mechanism that lets a relying party check, in real time, whether a specific certificate is valid or has been revoked. Instead of downloading a full list of revoked certificates, the client sends a query with the certificate's serial number and receives a signed response with the current status."},"2176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"Lamassu integrates its own OCSP responder that serves these queries by consulting the internal certificate database directly. No external component is required."},"2177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"When a client requests the status of a certificate, the responder locates the certificate by its serial number and determines its status from the internal record:"},"2178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate is active, the response indicates `Good`."},"2179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate has been revoked, the response indicates `Revoked` and includes the revocation timestamp and the RFC 5280 reason code."},"2180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the serial number is not found or the status is not recognizable, the response indicates `Unknown`."},"2181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The OCSP response is signed by the issuing CA of the queried certificate, using the cryptographic engine associated with that CA. Lamassu does not use a delegated OCSP signing certificate: the CA acts directly as the responder."},"2182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Each response has a validity window of 24 hours, reflected in the response's `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate` fields. Clients that cache responses must take this window into account when determining how long a response remains valid."},"2183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The OCSP responder URL is automatically embedded in the AIA (*Authority Information Access*) extension of every certificate issued by Lamassu. Clients that verify certificates can read this URL directly from the certificate without additional configuration."},"2184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The responder accepts both formats defined in RFC 6960:"},"2185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET /ocsp/{ocsp_request}` includes the OCSP request Base64url-encoded within the URL itself."},"2186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST /ocsp` sends the request in the body with `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"2187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Example query with `curl` using POST:"},"2188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and contains the OCSP response in DER format."},"2189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"From the certificates screen of Lamassu you can launch an OCSP request directly against the selected certificate with the **OCSP Check** action. This action shows the status returned by the responder without needing external tools."},"2190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960 - *X.509 Internet Public Key Infrastructure Online Certificate Status Protocol – OCSP*"},"2191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-24/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 5280 - *Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate and Certificate Revocation 