it for other principals."],[400,"A **policy** groups reusable permissions. It can be granted to several principals and can contain rules about Lamassu entities, rules about HTTP routes or both."],[399,"A **principal** connects a credential to Lamassu. It defines how to recognize an OIDC or X.509 identity and can be active or disabled."],[861,"A **single multiplexed endpoint** (`/.well-known/cmp/p/{id}`); the operation is determined by the message content"],[1542,"A &#x2A;*Device Management Service (DMS)** acts as the registration authority facing a fleet. It receives requests, applies the authentication policy and delegates issuance to the configured CA."],[1243,"A `nested` (RFC 4210 §5.1.3) is an envelope whose body contains one or more `PKIMessage`. With **a single** inner message it is *added protection* (RFC 9483 §5.2.2.1): an RA wraps and countersigns an already-protected device request; the outer header must copy the inner `transactionID` and `senderNonce`, the inner protection is verified and the request is processed normally. With **two or more** messages it is a batch (§5.2.2.2): the outer header carries new `transactionID`/`senderNonce`, the protection of each inner message is verified before any is processed and the responses come back wrapped in a `nested`, in the same order. A `ccr` inside a `nested` is not re-expedited, and nesting inside a batch is not supported."],[1508,"A background process monitors active VA roles. When the remaining validity of the current CRL falls below the configured watch period (*blind period*), the system requests the generation of a new CRL. This prevents the published CRL from expiring without a valid version available."],[2293,"A CA associated with the DMS."],[700,"A CA cannot issue certificates that outlive its own expiration date. Leave enough margin to renew or replace the authority without interrupting consumers."],[675,"A certification authority (CA) binds identities to public keys through signed certificates. In Lam